    "mapping_notes": "# tensorrt_llm__aux_kdaDecode_kdaDecode__sm_100f\n\n## Reference interface\n\nAll indices below are logical indices. Byte-level layout information from the\nsaved optimized input is retained in interface.json.\n\n| Parameter | Type | Logical shape | Role | Optimized counterpart |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| x_q | bf16 | 1 x 128 | input | x_q |\n| x_k | bf16 | 1 x 128 | input | x_k |\n| x_v | bf16 | 1 x 128 | input | x_v |\n| w_q | bf16 | 4 x 128 | input | w_q_t |\n| w_k | bf16 | 4 x 128 | input | w_k_t |\n| w_v | bf16 | 4 x 128 | input | w_v_t |\n| bias_q | bf16 | 128 | input | bias_q |\n| bias_k | bf16 | 128 | input | bias_k |\n| bias_v | bf16 | 128 | input | bias_v |\n| cs_q | bf16 | 1 x 128 x 3 | inout | cs_q |\n| cs_k | bf16 | 1 x 128 x 3 | inout | cs_k |\n| cs_v | bf16 | 1 x 128 x 3 | inout | cs_v |\n| a_log | float | 1 | input | a_log |\n| g | bf16 | 1 x 128 | input | g |\n| dt_bias | float | 128 | input | dt_bias |\n| beta | bf16 | 1 | input | beta |\n| onorm_g | bf16 | 1 x 128 | input | onorm_g |\n| onorm_weight | float | 128 | input | onorm_weight |\n| state | float | 1 x 128 x 128 | inout | state |\n| O | bf16 | 1 x 128 | output | out |\n| lower_bound | float | -5.0 | input | lower_bound |\n| scale | float | 0.08838834764831845 | input | scale |\n| epsilon | float | 1e-05 | input | epsilon |\n\n## Computation and mapping\n\nThis is the selected fixed B=H=HV=1, 128-key/128-value, width-four decode specialization.\nq/k/v = SiLU(bias + sum_{w=0..2} cache[w]*weight[w] + x*weight[3]).\nEach cache shifts left and receives x. q and k receive L2 normalization\nwith epsilon 1e-6; normalized q additionally receives scale.\ndecay[i] = exp(lower_bound * sigmoid(exp(a_log) * (g[i]+dt_bias[i]))).\nFor each value row j: Hdecay[j,i] = state[j,i]*decay[i];\ndelta[j] = sigmoid(beta)*(v[j]-sum_i Hdecay[j,i]*k[i]);\nstate'[j,i] = Hdecay[j,i]+delta[j]*k[i]; o[j]=sum_i state'[j,i]*q[i].\nO[j] = o[j]/sqrt(mean(o^2)+epsilon)*onorm_weight[j]*sigmoid(onorm_g[j]).\nstate is indexed [value,key], matching the source. w_* are source w_*_t\nwith axes [tap,channel]. Cache tensors have axes [batch,channel,history].\nThe selected static layout uses slot=batch and ignores dynamic state-index arrays.\nWith one batch, the source's slot-stride padding does not change element addresses.\n\n## Validation boundary\n\nCompiled to PTX and numerically checked on CPU. Not compared against an optimized\nGPU execution or proven equivalent. Precision/reduction-order differences follow\nthe mathematical contract in the top-level README.\n\n## Upstream\n\n- https://github.com/NVIDIA/TensorRT-LLM/blob/ef567dd9b8919f6ee8b2da1f6f6d0c90206a78f8/cpp/tensorrt_llm/kernels/kdaDecode/kdaDecode.cu\n- https://github.com/NVIDIA/TensorRT-LLM/blob/ef567dd9b8919f6ee8b2da1f6f6d0c90206a78f8/cpp/tensorrt_llm/kernels/kdaDecode/kdaDecode.h\n"
